  "configuration_id": "config_020",
  "reason": "The strongest result so far is config_018 (multimodal, multiprofile, pca_n2000, resnet50, avgpool, concat) at 0.619 acc / 0.610 F1, showing that multiprofile + avgpool aggregation is the dominant performance driver. The single most important untested design question on top of this best config is whether the aggregation strategy can be improved: avgpool is a simple, unparameterized operation, while a transformer aggregation learns attention-weighted interactions across profiles. config_020 changes exactly one variable (avgpool → transformer) relative to config_018, making it a clean controlled test. In contrast, config_019 (weighted fusion) is expected to yield only a marginal difference based on the near-identical singleprofile results (0.527 vs 0.523). If transformer aggregation significantly outperforms avgpool, it identifies a high-value architectural direction; if it does not, we confirm that simple averaging is sufficient and can redirect effort toward RNA/image encoder upgrades. Under a limited budget, this experiment maximizes information gain about a key architectural choice while staying in the proven high-performing region."
}

